# intermediate test - part #01

Let prop_post_masses be the vector of unnormalized posterior probability masses for a discrete parameter \theta taking values in \Theta=\{0,1,...,15\}
```{r}
# prop_post_masses
prop_post_masses = c(0.010, 0.010, 0.011, 0.016, 0.032, 0.075, 0.171, 0.356, 0.666, 1.128, 1.733, 2.412, 3.019, 3.327, 3.083, 2.141)

normalized_masses = prop_post_masses / sum(prop_post_masses)

data.frame(theta = 0:15,
           unnormalized = prop_post_masses,
           normalized = normalized_masses)
```

```{r}
# Vector of support
theta = 0:15
# Posterior mean
print("Posterior mean")
post_mean = sum(theta * normalized_masses)
post_mean
# Posterior median
cumulative_probs = cumsum(normalized_masses)
print("Posterior median")
post_median = theta[which.min(abs(cumulative_probs - 0.5))]
post_median
# Posterior mode
print("Posterior mode")
post_mode = theta[which.max(normalized_masses)]
post_mode
# 90% Equal-Tailed credible interval
print("Equal-Tailed credible interval")

print("Lower Bound")
lower_bound = theta[which(cumulative_probs >= 0.05)[1]]
lower_bound
print("Upper Bound")
upper_bound = theta[which(cumulative_probs >= 0.95)[1]]
upper_bound
```



