# intermediate test - part #02

Set as a seed for your simulation seed = 10397 and, immediately after, simulate 6 i.i.d. Bernoulli random variables with success probability equal to 0.4 using appropriately the function rbinom(...).

Which of the following is the conjugate family of prior distributions for the Bernoulli model?
```{r}
set.seed(10397)

# Simulate Bernoulli
y <- rbinom(6, 1, prob = 0.4)
n <- length(y)
successes <- sum(y)

# Prior: 
# Beta(1, 1)  uniform
alpha_prior <- 1
beta_prior <- 1

# Posterior: 
# Beta(1 + succ, 1 + fail)
alpha_post <- alpha_prior + successes
beta_post <- beta_prior + (n - successes)

# Simulate from posterior
posterior_samples <- rbeta(100000, alpha_post, beta_post)

library(HDInterval)

hpd_interval <- hdi(posterior_samples, credMass = 0.8)
hpd_interval  
```
```{r}
target_mean <- 0.8         # mean
target_prob <- 0.95        # P(\theta > 0.5)

# Loss function: squared error from both constraints
objective <- function(par) {
  alpha <- par[1]
  beta <- par[2]
  
  # mean of Beta
  mean_error <- (alpha / (alpha + beta) - target_mean)^2
  
  # tail probability above 0.5
  prob_error <- (1 - pbeta(0.5, alpha, beta) - target_prob)^2
  
  return(mean_error + prob_error)
}

# Optimize to minimize the total constraint violation
result <- optim(c(2, 2), objective, method = "L-BFGS-B", lower = c(0.1, 0.1))

# best parameters
result$par[1] # alpha
result$par[2] # beta
```

```{r}
